        "original_id": "d5e3e0fe-fff3-5cd0-81a6-8b475c740245",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Films: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons\n- Publications and Works: British Vogue, Les liaisons dangereuses, Les Liaisons dangereuses\n\nFacts:\n- In December 1985 and May 1986, Uma Thurman appeared on the covers of British Vogue.\n- In 1988, Uma Thurman starred in the film Dangerous Liaisons.\n- Dangerous Liaisons is a 1988 American historical drama film.\n- Dangerous Liaisons was based on Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses.\n- Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses was a theatrical adaptation of the 18th-century French novel Les Liaisons dangereuses by Pierre Choderlos de Laclos.\n- The film Mary Reilly reunited director Stephen Frears, screenwriter Christopher Hampton, and actors John Malkovich and Glenn Close.\n- Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, and Glenn Close had previously all been involved in the Oscar-winning 1988 film Dangerous Liaisons.",
